	<p>These are illustrative totals, not venue receipts. Actual rounding can differ by a few cents.</p>

	<p>For two people at a $200 menu each, tax plus a 20 percent pre-tax voluntary tip makes $515.50. The same meal with a 20 percent taxable service fee instead makes $522.60. If you add a 20 percent voluntary tip on top of that service fee, the total jumps to $602.60. That is the double-tip trap.</p>

	<p>Drinks change the math. A $200 meal plus a $60 sake pairing, with a 20 percent pre-tax tip, totals about $335.08 for one person. If the pairing is added after a service fee is calculated, the fee may or may not apply to it. Check the receipt.</p>

	<h2>Estimate your own bill</h2>

	<p>Enter your menu price, party size, and any drinks or extras. The calculator uses New York City sales tax of 8.875 percent. Set the tip to 0 if gratuity is included or tipping is not accepted. Set the service fee to 0 if there is none.</p>

